## Goal
Flag `return <expr>;` when the enclosing function's return type is `void`.

## Source
tm-editor-plus-plus `src/Dev/FindPatternCached.as` (2026-09-02). Game compile failed; `openplanet-lsp check` reported 0 errors (24 unrelated warnings).

## Repro
```angelscript
uint64 Helper() { return 1; }
void Dev_FindPatternCached(const string &in pat) {
    return Helper();
}
```

## Compiler (game-side)
```
Dev/FindPatternCached.as (21, 5) :  ERR : Can't return value when return type is 'void'
```

## LSP today
Silent. `openplanet-lsp check` on the full E++ tree accepted the file.

## Acceptance
- [ ] `return expr;` inside `void f()` is an error
- [ ] bare `return;` inside `void f()` stays silent
- [ ] `return expr;` whose type matches a non-void return type stays silent
- [ ] Regression fixture

## Notes
Sibling of the call-site miss: assigning that void call to a typed local (`uint64 fn = Dev_FindPatternCached(pat)`) is a separate game error (`Data type can't be 'void'`).